Subject: WPE on Phoenix: the frame watch, where each process's frame pipeline stands

A page can stop drawing while every main loop of the browser still runs, so neither a crash nor
the launcher's main-thread stall report says anything: the compositing thread stuck inside one
step of a frame, a rendering update waiting for tiles still being painted, a frame the UI process
never answered with a frame-done, the UI waiting for the compositor's frame callback, or no display
refresh reaching requestAnimationFrame (b35-gate2: a WebGL page froze ~15 s in, silently).

Each of those places records its progress in PhoenixFrameWatch.h (a header-only set of
relaxed atomics, OS(PHOENIX) only): the ThreadedCompositor's scheduling state and the step of the
frame it is in, the frames sent and done, the swap chain's targets, the tiles pending, the
LayerTreeHost's rendering updates and its wait for the renderer; in the UI process the backing
store's frames (received, handed to the view, called back) and the DisplayLink's ticks and
observers. wpe_phoenix_frame_watch() describes one process's half as a line and says which wait,
if any, has lasted longer than a limit. It reads atomics only: the caller is the launcher's
watchdog thread, and a stuck thread may hold any lock.

  frame-watch kind=render|tiles|frame-done|no-frame|scheduled|renderer|none compositor state=..
  frame-watch kind=ui-pending|ui-callback|none backing-store received=.. display-link ticks=..

